{
  "$schema": "https://jxsuite.com/schema/v1",
  "$id": "StylebookPopover",
  "tagName": "main",
  "$elements": [
    {
      "$ref": "../components/jx-checkbox.json"
    },
    {
      "$ref": "../components/jx-popover.json"
    }
  ],
  "state": {
    "grid": true,
    "guides": false,
    "rulers": false
  },
  "style": {
    "fontFamily": "var(--jx-font-sans)",
    "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)",
    "color": "var(--jx-fg)",
    "background": "var(--jx-bg)",
    "padding": "var(--jx-space-6)",
    "minHeight": "100vh",
    "& > h1": {
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-lg)",
      "fontWeight": "600",
      "margin": "0 0 var(--jx-space-5)"
    },
    "& > h2": {
      "fontSize": "var(--jx-text-md)",
      "fontWeight": "600",
      "color": "var(--jx-fg-dim)",
      "margin": "var(--jx-space-6) 0 var(--jx-space-3)"
    },
    "& > p": {
      "color": "var(--jx-fg-dim)",
      "margin": "0 0 var(--jx-space-5)"
    },
    "& button": {
      "font": "inherit",
      "color": "var(--jx-fg)",
      "background": "var(--jx-bg-input)",
      "border": "1px solid var(--jx-border)",
      "borderRadius": "var(--jx-radius-sm)",
      "padding": "var(--jx-space-2) var(--jx-space-4)"
    }
  },
  "children": [
    {
      "tagName": "h1",
      "textContent": "jx-popover"
    },
    {
      "tagName": "p",
      "textContent": "A panel is a native auto popover with one unnamed slot. Light dismiss, Escape and focus restoration are the platform's; the element adds no key of its own. It is placed by measured viewport coordinates, and the gap between it and its trigger is the --jx-popover-offset token."
    },
    {
      "tagName": "h2",
      "textContent": "A named panel of controls"
    },
    {
      "tagName": "p",
      "textContent": "A panel holding controls MUST set label: it becomes a named role=\"group\", so the panel announces a boundary on entry. An unnamed group is invisible to every gate, which is why the element cannot leave this to the consumer's judgement alone."
    },
    {
      "tagName": "button",
      "attributes": {
        "popovertarget": "stylebook-popover-grid"
      },
      "textContent": "Grid options…"
    },
    {
      "tagName": "jx-popover",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "stylebook-popover-grid"
      },
      "$props": {
        "label": "Grid options",
        "x": 24,
        "y": 200,
        "arrow": true
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "tagName": "jx-checkbox",
          "$props": {
            "checked": {
              "$ref": "#/state/grid"
            },
            "label": "Show grid"
          }
        },
        {
          "tagName": "jx-checkbox",
          "$props": {
            "checked": {
              "$ref": "#/state/guides"
            },
            "label": "Show guides"
          }
        },
        {
          "tagName": "jx-checkbox",
          "$props": {
            "checked": {
              "$ref": "#/state/rulers"
            },
            "label": "Show rulers"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tagName": "h2",
      "textContent": "How a page opens one"
    },
    {
      "tagName": "p",
      "textContent": "The trigger above is a raw <button popovertarget>, which every caller of the overlay lints accepts. So is $props: { popovertarget } on a kit button, because the lints read a node's attributes and never its $props. The third spelling, popovertarget in a kit button's attributes, DEPENDS ON THE CALLER: the rule judges the tag the document writes rather than the tag the definition renders, so a caller that names the kit's invoker tags (Studio does) reports nothing, and a caller that names none reports invoker-not-button."
    }
  ]
}
